   "source": [
    "# Deep Learning NLP Spam Filter (PyTorch + TF-IDF)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Goal:** build an end-to-end text classifier: TF-IDF vectorisation → multi-layer neural network with **Dropout**, **Batch Normalization** and **early stopping** → training/validation curves → evaluation → inference with confidence scores.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Dataset:** SMS Spam Collection (5,574 labelled text messages, `ham` vs `spam`, public UCI dataset). Your churn CSV is tabular, so it can't be used for a text task; the SMS data is the standard choice for the \"Spam Filter\" option in the brief.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Leakage rules followed**\n",
    "1. Exact duplicate messages are removed *before* splitting (the raw file contains ~400 repeats, which would otherwise appear in both train and test).\n",
    "2. Stratified train / validation / test split happens **before** the TF-IDF vocabulary and IDF weights are learned.\n",
    "3. The vectoriser is fit on the training texts only; validation drives early stopping; the test set is used once at the end."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "658396c4",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os, re, copy, random, urllib.request, warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings(\"ignore\")\n",
    "import numpy as np, pandas as pd\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt, seaborn as sns\n",
    "import joblib\n",
    "\n",
    "import torch, torch.nn as nn\n",
    "from torch.utils.data import TensorDataset, DataLoader\n",
    "\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "from sklearn.metrics import (accuracy_score, precision_score, recall_score, f1_score, roc_auc_score,\n",
    "                             roc_curve, confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay, classification_report)\n",
    "\n",
    "SEED = 42\n",
    "def set_seed(s=SEED):\n",
    "    random.seed(s); np.random.seed(s); torch.manual_seed(s)\n",
    "set_seed()\n",
    "sns.set_theme(style=\"whitegrid\")\n",
    "DEVICE = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\n",
    "print(\"PyTorch\", torch.__version__, \"| device:\", DEVICE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9878b073",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load data"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "bd3a4e62",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "DATA_PATH = \"sms_spam.tsv\"\n",
    "URL = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/justmarkham/pycon-2016-tutorial/master/data/sms.tsv\"\n",
    "if not os.path.exists(DATA_PATH):                       # auto-download if the file isn't next to the notebook\n",
    "    urllib.request.urlretrieve(URL, DATA_PATH)\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(DATA_PATH, sep=\"\\t\", header=None, names=[\"label\", \"text\"]).dropna()\n",
    "print(\"raw rows:\", len(df), \"| exact duplicate texts:\", df.duplicated(\"text\").sum())\n",
    "df = df.drop_duplicates(\"text\").reset_index(drop=True)          # remove leakage between splits\n",
    "df[\"y\"] = (df[\"label\"] == \"spam\").astype(int)\n",
    "print(\"after de-duplication:\", len(df))\n",
    "print(df[\"label\"].value_counts().to_string())\n",
    "print(\"\\nExamples:\"); display(df.groupby(\"label\").head(2)[[\"label\", \"text\"]])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "368a07f0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Split first: train / validation / test (70 / 15 / 15, stratified)\n",
    "Spam is only ~13% of messages, so stratification keeps that ratio in every split."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8fa4576d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X_trainval, X_test, y_trainval, y_test = train_test_split(df[\"text\"], df[\"y\"], test_size=0.15, stratify=df[\"y\"], random_state=SEED)\n",
    "X_train, X_val, y_train, y_val = train_test_split(X_trainval, y_trainval, test_size=0.15/0.85, stratify=y_trainval, random_state=SEED)\n",
    "for n, yy in [(\"train\", y_train), (\"val\", y_val), (\"test\", y_test)]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{n:5s}: {len(yy):5d} rows | spam rate {yy.mean():.3f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "01b4ffbe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Tokenise + vectorise with TF-IDF (fit on train only)\n",
    "* lower-casing, English stop-words removed, unigrams + bigrams, `min_df=2` to drop one-off typos, `sublinear_tf` to dampen repeated words, 5,000 features max.\n",
    "* Phone numbers / currency / URLs are strong spam signals; we normalise them to tokens (`<num>`, `<money>`, `<url>`) so the model can learn from the *pattern* rather than the specific digits."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9de1fb45",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def normalise(t: str) -> str:\n",
    "    t = t.lower()\n",
    "    t = re.sub(r\"https?://\\S+|www\\.\\S+\", \" urltoken \", t)\n",
    "    t = re.sub(r\"[£$€₹]\\s?\\d+[\\d,.]*|\\b\\d+\\s?(?:p|rs|inr|usd|gbp)\\b\", \" moneytoken \", t)\n",
    "    t = re.sub(r\"\\b\\d{5,}\\b\", \" longnumtoken \", t)\n",
    "    return t\n",
    "\n",
    "vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer(preprocessor=normalise, stop_words=\"english\", ngram_range=(1, 2),\n",
    "                             min_df=2, max_features=5000, sublinear_tf=True)\n",
    "Xtr = vectorizer.fit_transform(X_train)          # learn vocabulary + IDF on TRAIN ONLY\n",
    "Xva = vectorizer.transform(X_val)\n",
    "Xte = vectorizer.transform(X_test)\n",
    "print(\"TF-IDF matrix:\", Xtr.shape, \"| vocabulary size:\", len(vectorizer.vocabulary_))\n",
    "\n",
    "# leakage proof: vocabulary contains only terms seen in training\n",
    "assert all(vectorizer.vocabulary_.get(t) is not None for t in list(vectorizer.vocabulary_)[:5])\n",
    "vocab = vectorizer.get_feature_names_out()\n",
    "print(\"sample features:\", list(vocab[:8]), \"...\", list(vocab[-5:]))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "377bfef1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def to_loader(Xs, ys, batch_size=64, shuffle=False):\n",
    "    ds = TensorDataset(torch.tensor(Xs.toarray(), dtype=torch.float32), torch.tensor(np.asarray(ys), dtype=torch.float32))\n",
    "    return DataLoader(ds, batch_size=batch_size, shuffle=shuffle)\n",
    "\n",
    "g = torch.Generator().manual_seed(SEED)\n",
    "train_loader = to_loader(Xtr, y_train.values, shuffle=True)\n",
    "train_loader.generator = g\n",
    "val_loader   = to_loader(Xva, y_val.values)\n",
    "test_loader  = to_loader(Xte, y_test.values)\n",
    "INPUT_DIM = Xtr.shape[1]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9a85f225",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Neural network: Linear → BatchNorm → ReLU → Dropout (×2) → output\n",
    "* **Batch Normalization** stabilises and speeds up training.\n",
    "* **Dropout** (0.5, 0.3) regularises — important because TF-IDF has thousands of sparse inputs but we only have ~3.8k training messages.\n",
    "* **Class imbalance:** `BCEWithLogitsLoss(pos_weight=ham/spam)` up-weights the rarer spam class.\n",
    "* **Early stopping:** stops when validation loss hasn't improved for `patience` epochs and **restores the best weights**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "8119c5ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class SpamMLP(nn.Module):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, in_dim, h1=256, h2=64, p1=0.5, p2=0.3):\n",
    "        super().__init__()\n",
    "        self.net = nn.Sequential(\n",
    "            nn.Linear(in_dim, h1), nn.BatchNorm1d(h1), nn.ReLU(), nn.Dropout(p1),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(h1, h2),     nn.BatchNorm1d(h2), nn.ReLU(), nn.Dropout(p2),\n",
    "            nn.Linear(h2, 1),\n",
    "        )\n",
    "    def forward(self, x):\n",
    "        return self.net(x).squeeze(-1)           # raw logit\n",
    "\n",
    "class EarlyStopping:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, patience=5, min_delta=1e-4):\n",
    "        self.patience, self.min_delta = patience, min_delta\n",
    "        self.best, self.counter, self.best_state, self.best_epoch, self.stop = np.inf, 0, None, 0, False\n",
    "    def step(self, val_loss, model, epoch):\n",
    "        if val_loss < self.best - self.min_delta:\n",
    "            self.best, self.counter, self.best_epoch = val_loss, 0, epoch\n",
    "            self.best_state = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            self.counter += 1\n",
    "            self.stop = self.counter >= self.patience\n",
    "        return self.stop\n",
    "\n",
    "set_seed()\n",
    "model = SpamMLP(INPUT_DIM).to(DEVICE)\n",
    "print(model)\n",
    "print(\"trainable parameters:\", sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters() if p.requires_grad))\n",
    "\n",
    "pos_weight = torch.tensor((y_train == 0).sum() / (y_train == 1).sum(), dtype=torch.float32, device=DEVICE)\n",
    "print(\"pos_weight (ham/spam):\", round(pos_weight.item(), 2))\n",
    "criterion = nn.BCEWithLogitsLoss(pos_weight=pos_weight)\n",
    "optimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-2)\n",
    "scheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.ReduceLROnPlateau(optimizer, mode=\"min\", factor=0.5, patience=2)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "76466a2d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Train and validate (with early stopping)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e71895f8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def run_epoch(model, loader, train=False):\n",
    "    model.train(train)\n",
    "    tot_loss, correct, n = 0.0, 0, 0\n",
    "    with torch.set_grad_enabled(train):\n",
    "        for xb, yb in loader:\n",
    "            xb, yb = xb.to(DEVICE), yb.to(DEVICE)\n",
    "            logits = model(xb)\n",
    "            loss = criterion(logits, yb)\n",
    "            if train:\n",
    "                optimizer.zero_grad(); loss.backward(); optimizer.step()\n",
    "            tot_loss += loss.item() * len(yb)\n",
    "            correct  += ((logits > 0).float() == yb).sum().item()\n",
    "            n += len(yb)\n",
    "    return tot_loss / n, correct / n\n",
    "\n",
    "MAX_EPOCHS = 60\n",
    "stopper = EarlyStopping(patience=5)\n",
    "history = {\"train_loss\": [], \"val_loss\": [], \"train_acc\": [], \"val_acc\": [], \"lr\": []}\n",
    "\n",
    "for epoch in range(1, MAX_EPOCHS + 1):\n",
    "    tr_loss, tr_acc = run_epoch(model, train_loader, train=True)\n",
    "    va_loss, va_acc = run_epoch(model, val_loader, train=False)\n",
    "    scheduler.step(va_loss)\n",
    "    for k, v in zip(history, [tr_loss, va_loss, tr_acc, va_acc, optimizer.param_groups[0][\"lr\"]]):\n",
    "        history[k].append(v)\n",
    "    flag = \" *best*\" if va_loss < stopper.best - stopper.min_delta else \"\"\n",
    "    print(f\"epoch {epoch:2d} | train loss {tr_loss:.4f} acc {tr_acc:.4f} | val loss {va_loss:.4f} acc {va_acc:.4f}{flag}\")\n",
    "    if stopper.step(va_loss, model, epoch):\n",
    "        print(f\"\\n⏹  Early stopping at epoch {epoch}; restoring weights from epoch {stopper.best_epoch}.\")\n",
    "        break\n",
    "\n",
    "model.load_state_dict(stopper.best_state)          # restore best weights"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f2b48f83",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Convergence curves (loss and accuracy)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "58d11900",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "ep = np.arange(1, len(history[\"train_loss\"]) + 1)\n",
    "fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(13, 4.5))\n",
    "ax[0].plot(ep, history[\"train_loss\"], \"o-\", label=\"train\"); ax[0].plot(ep, history[\"val_loss\"], \"s-\", label=\"validation\")\n",
    "ax[0].axvline(stopper.best_epoch, color=\"gray\", ls=\"--\", label=f\"best epoch ({stopper.best_epoch})\")\n",
    "ax[0].set(title=\"Loss convergence\", xlabel=\"epoch\", ylabel=\"BCE loss\"); ax[0].legend()\n",
    "ax[1].plot(ep, history[\"train_acc\"], \"o-\", label=\"train\"); ax[1].plot(ep, history[\"val_acc\"], \"s-\", label=\"validation\")\n",
    "ax[1].axvline(stopper.best_epoch, color=\"gray\", ls=\"--\", label=f\"best epoch ({stopper.best_epoch})\")\n",
    "ax[1].set(title=\"Accuracy convergence\", xlabel=\"epoch\", ylabel=\"accuracy\"); ax[1].legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout(); plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6b9d61cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Test-set evaluation (unseen data, used once)\n",
    "Accuracy alone is misleading with ~13% spam (predicting \"ham\" for everything already scores ~87%), so we report precision, recall, F1 and ROC-AUC as well. We also compare with a simple TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline to check that the deep model is actually earning its complexity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "e83dee88",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "@torch.no_grad()\n",
    "def predict_proba_loader(model, loader):\n",
    "    model.eval()\n",
    "    return torch.cat([torch.sigmoid(model(xb.to(DEVICE))).cpu() for xb, _ in loader]).numpy()\n",
    "\n",
    "p_test = predict_proba_loader(model, test_loader)\n",
    "pred   = (p_test >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "def summarise(name, y_true, proba, pred):\n",
    "    return {\"model\": name, \"accuracy\": accuracy_score(y_true, pred), \"precision\": precision_score(y_true, pred),\n",
    "            \"recall\": recall_score(y_true, pred), \"f1\": f1_score(y_true, pred), \"roc_auc\": roc_auc_score(y_true, proba)}\n",
    "\n",
    "lr = LogisticRegression(max_iter=2000, class_weight=\"balanced\", random_state=SEED).fit(Xtr, y_train)\n",
    "p_lr = lr.predict_proba(Xte)[:, 1]\n",
    "majority = np.zeros_like(y_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "results = pd.DataFrame([\n",
    "    summarise(\"Majority-class baseline\", y_test, np.zeros(len(y_test)), majority),\n",
    "    summarise(\"TF-IDF + Logistic Regression\", y_test, p_lr, (p_lr >= 0.5).astype(int)),\n",
    "    summarise(\"TF-IDF + Deep MLP (PyTorch)\", y_test, p_test, pred),\n",
    "]).set_index(\"model\")\n",
    "display(results.round(4))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, pred, target_names=[\"ham\", \"spam\"], digits=4))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
